{
  "edit": "Rotate the camera 90 degrees to the left inside the same bathroom and render the new view.",
  "references": {
    "image 1": "the bathroom from the current camera position: use it for materials, tile pattern, colors, lighting and the wall with the doorway",
    "image 2": "the same bathroom from another angle: use it for the layout of the back wall, the window, the glass shower and the pink vanity unit on the left wall; the towel radiator at its right edge is the same single radiator as in image 1",
    "image 3": "same view as image 2, for fine details"
  },
  "scene": "A long, spacious modern bathroom seen from floor level, the wide back wall facing the camera at a distance. The room contains exactly one white towel radiator, mounted on the right wall right next to the corner with the window wall.",
  "lighting": "Neutral soft lighting identical to image 1, soft daylight through the window, a narrow strip of warm light from the hallway through the doorway.",
  "composition": "Right third: the doorway wall recedes in steep perspective, the open doorway seen edge-on as a thin white frame over an empty threshold, and further back, close to the window corner, the single white towel radiator seen in profile. Center: the back wall with the white window and small potted plant on the sill, the curved glass shower with rain head and rounded shelves, the terracotta stool and green bath mat. Left edge: the end of the pink floating vanity unit with its round lit mirror, partly cropped by the frame.",
  "camera": {
    "angle": "level camera very close to the floor, 10 to 15 cm high",
    "lens": "wide-angle, 16:9",
    "depth_of_field": "sharp focus throughout, same as image 1"
  },
  "style": "Photorealistic interior photograph, same grain, sharpness and color rendering as image 1, clean image.",
  "background": "Olive-green lower wall tiles, white upper tiles with green vertical accents, large grey floor tiles, white ceiling with recessed spots. The back wall and the left wall are plain tiled surfaces around the window, the shower and the vanity.",
  "keep_unchanged": "One single towel radiator in the whole room, next to the window corner. Tile colors and pattern, door frame, radiator design, shower design, window design, vanity color and shape, the overall palette of images 1 and 2."
}
